WEBVTT

00:00:01.366 --> 00:00:02.491
[PHOENIX] Maya and I
traveled to Hazakura Temple

00:00:02.575 --> 00:00:04.575
in the snowy mountains,
so she could further

00:00:04.658 --> 00:00:06.033
her spiritual training.

00:00:06.116 --> 00:00:08.616
But tragedy struck
when children's book author

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.700
Elise Deauxnim was murdered.

00:00:10.783 --> 00:00:12.616
Lightning set Dusky
Bridge on fire,

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:15.075
stranding Maya on
the other side of the river.

00:00:15.158 --> 00:00:18.325
Failing to cross over and save
her, I ended up stranded, too--

00:00:18.408 --> 00:00:19.991
in a hospital bed.

00:00:20.075 --> 00:00:22.700
The police arrested
Sister Iris for the murder.

00:00:22.783 --> 00:00:25.825
The defendant is a secretive nun
who bears an uncanny resemblance

00:00:25.908 --> 00:00:29.200
to Dahlia Hawthorne,
whose face I could never forget.

00:00:29.283 --> 00:00:31.408
As a favor to me,
Miles agreed to argue

00:00:31.491 --> 00:00:32.866
her case at trial.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:34.658
Things looked bleak,
but when his fellow

00:00:34.741 --> 00:00:38.283
Von Karma protégé, Franziska,
had him backed into a corner,

00:00:38.366 --> 00:00:39.950
a voice cried foul!

00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:41.116
[BUTZ]
Objection!

00:00:44.616 --> 00:00:45.658
[MILES]
Larry!

00:00:45.741 --> 00:00:47.575
Sorry, Vincent Van Bro,
but you can

00:00:47.658 --> 00:00:49.075
call me Laurice Deauxnim.

00:00:49.158 --> 00:00:50.491
Did he say Deauxnim?

00:00:50.575 --> 00:00:52.616
[BUTZ] Everything that
happened that night.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:54.116
I saw it all.

00:00:55.616 --> 00:00:57.700
And if I can save
my beautiful little flower,

00:00:57.783 --> 00:01:00.533
I'll paint you a masterpiece
with my testimony!

00:02:35.241 --> 00:02:37.616
So you say
you name is Laurice Deauxnim.

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:38.700
That right?

00:02:38.783 --> 00:02:40.783
Your Honor.
This man was apprentice

00:02:40.866 --> 00:02:42.325
to the late Ms. Deauxnim.

00:02:42.408 --> 00:02:44.741
That night, he was staying in a
small cabin near the scene.

00:02:44.825 --> 00:02:46.866
I was having a ball
in Heavenly Hall!

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:48.200
That's not relevant.

00:02:48.283 --> 00:02:49.533
What about the night
in question?

00:02:49.616 --> 00:02:51.491
Hey, I'm just
tryin' to set the scene.

00:02:51.575 --> 00:02:52.866
I'm gonna tell you my story,

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:54.533
'cause I ain't runnin'
from the truth!

00:02:54.616 --> 00:02:56.366
[MILES] You say that,
yet you've proven you'll run

00:02:56.450 --> 00:02:58.616
from my questions.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.533
[JUDGE 204A] Well, sir,
please begin your testimony.

00:03:03.741 --> 00:03:05.950
Iris did take the
snowmobile that night.

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:08.325
But it wasn't
to commit any crime.

00:03:08.408 --> 00:03:10.450
No, she did it to
give us all a warning.

00:03:10.533 --> 00:03:12.616
We needed to know
that dinner was ready!

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:13.658
[JUDGE 204A]
Dinner?

00:03:17.325 --> 00:03:19.866
Yeah! She was
like "come and get it."

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:21.825
Oh, man, she looked super-cool!

00:03:23.866 --> 00:03:25.241
A little later that night,

00:03:25.325 --> 00:03:27.950
I was in the cabin cranking
out a true work of art.

00:03:28.033 --> 00:03:29.158
Well, in my dreams.

00:03:29.241 --> 00:03:31.491
Say what? Can you translate?

00:03:31.575 --> 00:03:32.950
I'd wager he
means he dozed off

00:03:33.033 --> 00:03:34.491
while painting or drawing.

00:03:34.575 --> 00:03:35.866
Suddenly, crashentino!

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:37.575
Pow! It was hella loud.

00:03:37.658 --> 00:03:40.033
Totally scared the
living crap outta me.

00:03:40.116 --> 00:03:42.950
But then I saw that
creaky ol' bridge up in flames.

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:44.366
I rushed over to check it out,

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.658
and that's when I ran
into my buddy Nick.

00:03:46.741 --> 00:03:48.950
Was the bridge still intact?

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:51.783
Well, I wouldn't have set
foot on it if you paid me to.

00:03:51.866 --> 00:03:53.658
The thing was up in flames.

00:03:53.741 --> 00:03:55.200
But Nick was feeling brave.

00:03:55.283 --> 00:03:57.491
He tried to cross it and
tumbled right into the gorge.

00:03:57.575 --> 00:03:58.491
Is that true?

00:03:58.575 --> 00:03:59.491
[gasps]

00:03:59.575 --> 00:04:01.450
He didn't sustain any injuries.

00:04:01.533 --> 00:04:03.658
Caught a nasty cold, however.

00:04:03.741 --> 00:04:06.408
He either has the
most incredible or rotten luck.

00:04:06.491 --> 00:04:08.741
It's almost impossible to tell.

00:04:08.825 --> 00:04:11.575
So Larry.
According to police records,

00:04:11.658 --> 00:04:14.241
they received a call about
the incident at 11:30.

00:04:14.325 --> 00:04:16.200
You were the one who made
that call, were you not?

00:04:16.283 --> 00:04:18.908
[BUTZ] Yeah! That's exactly
what I shoulda done, right?

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:20.825
Lightning struck Dusky
bridge at approximately

00:04:20.908 --> 00:04:22.700
10:45 that night.

00:04:22.783 --> 00:04:24.950
Can you explain why
there was a 45 minute gap

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:25.950
before you called?

00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:26.991
[gasps]

00:04:27.075 --> 00:04:28.616
You said you
were staying in a cabin

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:32.283
a stone's throw away.
So why did you wait to call?

00:04:32.366 --> 00:04:33.491
Uh, let's see...

00:04:33.575 --> 00:04:34.825
Well... I, uh...

00:04:34.908 --> 00:04:35.866
What the hell?!

00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:37.033
Answer the question!

00:04:37.116 --> 00:04:38.241
I wasn't just sitting there!

00:04:38.325 --> 00:04:39.908
I'm an artiste, ya know?

00:04:39.991 --> 00:04:41.408
It was divine inspiration!

00:04:41.491 --> 00:04:43.283
I just had to make some art!

00:04:43.366 --> 00:04:44.741
So, you were painting?

00:04:44.825 --> 00:04:46.325
The bridge wasn't
the only thing burning,

00:04:46.408 --> 00:04:48.741
my artistic spirit
was also on fire!

00:04:48.825 --> 00:04:51.491
So you were just drawing
over by the burning bridge

00:04:51.575 --> 00:04:53.325
until the moment Phoenix
Wright showed up?

00:04:53.408 --> 00:04:56.408
Well, duh! I said that
it was divine inspiration!

00:04:56.491 --> 00:04:58.408
The bridge was giving
up its life for my art!

00:04:58.491 --> 00:05:00.491
What a selfish thing to say!

00:05:00.575 --> 00:05:01.700
[BOTH gasp]

00:05:03.283 --> 00:05:05.325
Okay. Then show
us your creation.

00:05:05.408 --> 00:05:06.908
Why?

00:05:06.991 --> 00:05:08.991
I'm not sure that the piece is
quite ready for exhibition yet.

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:10.950
When I saw you
yesterday, you said you

00:05:11.033 --> 00:05:13.033
witnessed something "bonkers."

00:05:13.116 --> 00:05:15.408
Does this artwork have
anything to do with that?

00:05:15.491 --> 00:05:16.533
[gasps]

00:05:19.283 --> 00:05:20.700
Wow.

00:05:20.783 --> 00:05:22.700
I've actually been dreaming
about how this would happen.

00:05:22.783 --> 00:05:24.450
But I never imagined
Laurice Deauxnim

00:05:24.533 --> 00:05:26.158
would make his grand debut in--

00:05:26.241 --> 00:05:28.741
--Ow! Man, that stings! Stop!
--Just show it to us, now!

00:05:28.825 --> 00:05:31.283
[BUTZ growls] I hope your
brains can handle it.

00:05:31.366 --> 00:05:32.616
Behold!

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:35.616
The world, as seen through
my unique artistic eye!

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:37.866
♪ Da-da-da-dah! ♪

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:39.450
It's unique.

00:05:39.533 --> 00:05:41.450
But could you tell us what the
thing flying over the bridge is?

00:05:41.533 --> 00:05:43.825
It's exactly what
it looks like, old pal.

00:05:43.908 --> 00:05:45.325
You're going to have
to explain it.

00:05:45.408 --> 00:05:46.658
Anybody with working eyeballs

00:05:46.741 --> 00:05:48.575
can clearly see that's Iris!

00:05:50.325 --> 00:05:52.950
[BUTZ] I still can't believe
she flew like that.

00:05:53.033 --> 00:05:56.241
A beautiful girl like her needs
to take better care of herself,

00:05:56.325 --> 00:05:58.908
or something's gonna happen
to ruin those looks.

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:01.158
[CROWD gasping]

00:06:01.241 --> 00:06:03.158
Witness! Are
you really testifying to

00:06:03.241 --> 00:06:05.783
this ridiculous claim that
the defendant was seen

00:06:05.866 --> 00:06:07.116
flying over the bridge?

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.575
Yeah, and now
you understand why--

00:06:08.658 --> 00:06:09.783
[yelps]

00:06:09.866 --> 00:06:11.825
This all sounds like
something from a dream.

00:06:11.908 --> 00:06:14.533
That's why I had to whip you.
To make sure everyone's awake.

00:06:14.616 --> 00:06:17.491
If you're really worried
about that, then whip yourself!

00:06:17.575 --> 00:06:19.866
So, Iris doesn't actually
need a snowmobile

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:21.616
to get from place to place.

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:24.200
'Cause it turns out that
gorgeous angel can fly!

00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:26.283
Well, this is hardly believable.

00:06:26.366 --> 00:06:28.075
[MILES]
Is this how he sees the world?

00:06:28.158 --> 00:06:29.908
I should never have
let him speak.

00:06:29.991 --> 00:06:31.200
[FRANZISKA]
Control your witness!

00:06:31.283 --> 00:06:33.450
If you're able, please
bring this unhinged fool

00:06:33.533 --> 00:06:34.575
back down to Earth.

00:06:34.658 --> 00:06:35.825
Wait, you're asking me?

00:06:35.908 --> 00:06:36.908
Yes, of course.

00:06:36.991 --> 00:06:39.116
This, "artiste."
So he's your friend?

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:41.325
If true, you're
a fool's accessory.

00:06:41.408 --> 00:06:42.325
[MILES gasps]

00:06:42.408 --> 00:06:43.741
You heard the judge, Edgy.

00:06:43.825 --> 00:06:44.866
An accessory!

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:46.533
[MILES]
What the hell is going on here?!

00:06:46.616 --> 00:06:49.033
I mean, he's gotta be
high on something.

00:06:51.741 --> 00:06:54.116
So just to clarify
things once again.

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:56.491
You saw Sister Iris
flying over the bridge?

00:06:56.575 --> 00:06:57.575
Yeah.

00:06:57.658 --> 00:06:58.950
I was watching the
fire for a second,

00:06:59.033 --> 00:07:00.408
and then, all of a sudden...
Whoosh!

00:07:00.491 --> 00:07:02.866
She was pulling like,
30 feet of air and a sweet arc.

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:04.366
I see.

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:05.783
And do you happen to know where
she may have been flying?

00:07:05.866 --> 00:07:07.658
I got no clue,
I just kinda caught a glimpse

00:07:07.741 --> 00:07:09.116
of her through the window.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:11.950
And so, I started creating
my rendition like a madman!

00:07:12.033 --> 00:07:14.116
But how can you be
so sure it was the defendant

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:18.700
that you saw? You couldn't have
had a clear view from the cabin.

00:07:18.783 --> 00:07:20.575
[chuckles]

00:07:20.658 --> 00:07:22.616
You do realize who
you're talking to?

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:23.783
I'm a Deauxnim.

00:07:23.866 --> 00:07:25.866
Nothing escapes my artist's eye!

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:28.158
Including proof she
was the person I saw!

00:07:28.241 --> 00:07:29.200
There's proof?

00:07:29.283 --> 00:07:31.575
[BUTZ chuckles]

00:07:31.658 --> 00:07:33.658
After Nick went
whizzing into the gorge,

00:07:33.741 --> 00:07:34.950
I called the cops.

00:07:35.033 --> 00:07:36.825
I came back to where
the bridge used to be

00:07:36.908 --> 00:07:38.408
and saw something nutty.

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:39.700
"Nutty," how?

00:07:39.783 --> 00:07:41.283
I'll show ya!

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:45.491
So, what is this?
A crystal sphere?

00:07:45.575 --> 00:07:46.575
Or what?

00:07:46.658 --> 00:07:47.825
Pretty sure it's
the thing from Iris's

00:07:47.908 --> 00:07:49.491
weird hoodie that she wears.

00:07:49.575 --> 00:07:52.116
I think that it probably
fell off when she landed.

00:07:53.408 --> 00:07:56.366
[FRANZISKA] Well. Her headwear
did have a crystal sphere on it.

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:59.950
[JUDGE 204A gasps] There's a
red stain on this, right there.

00:08:00.033 --> 00:08:01.658
I believe that
it might be blood.

00:08:01.741 --> 00:08:03.075
There are bloodstains on it?

00:08:03.158 --> 00:08:05.158
[CROWD gasping]

00:08:05.241 --> 00:08:08.033
That's why I was worried
about her doing dangerous stuff.

00:08:08.116 --> 00:08:09.450
Poor thing...

00:08:09.533 --> 00:08:12.366
She must've hit the ground
too hard when she landed.

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:13.575
[MILES]
Objection!

00:08:13.658 --> 00:08:16.075
[BUTZ whimpers, yelps]

00:08:16.158 --> 00:08:17.825
After your testimony,

00:08:17.908 --> 00:08:20.033
there is one fact that
I'm absolutely certain of.

00:08:20.116 --> 00:08:21.825
[BUTZ]
Yeah? Well, what is it?

00:08:21.908 --> 00:08:24.116
The person that
you depicted in this work...

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:25.575
...could not be the defendant!

00:08:25.658 --> 00:08:27.325
Uh... No?

00:08:27.408 --> 00:08:28.575
The night of the crime.

00:08:28.658 --> 00:08:31.116
Sister Iris's head was
completely uncovered.

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:32.783
But as seen in this picture.

00:08:32.866 --> 00:08:35.450
[JUDGE 204A] You can tell
she has the hood on right there.

00:08:35.533 --> 00:08:37.033
What?

00:08:37.116 --> 00:08:39.575
Oh, really? But how in
the world would you know that?

00:08:39.658 --> 00:08:42.325
I mean, you weren't even at
the temple that night, man.

00:08:42.408 --> 00:08:44.200
Because I talked to
the person to whom she had

00:08:44.283 --> 00:08:48.033
earlier given her hood.
She gave it to Phoenix Wright.

00:08:48.116 --> 00:08:49.991
What? So Nick had it?

00:08:50.075 --> 00:08:51.575
I believe that
he may have been

00:08:51.658 --> 00:08:54.741
the hooded figure you painted.
He was wearing one, after all.

00:08:54.825 --> 00:08:58.575
[BUTZ growls]
Why does he always do this?

00:08:58.658 --> 00:09:01.491
It was, like, totally obvious
I was into her!

00:09:01.575 --> 00:09:04.033
Calm yourself!
So explain the crystal sphere!

00:09:04.116 --> 00:09:06.200
It was discovered at
the foot of Dusky Bridge.

00:09:06.283 --> 00:09:08.200
And there're clearly
bloodstains on it!

00:09:09.575 --> 00:09:10.616
That one is too big.

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:11.908
[gasps]

00:09:11.991 --> 00:09:13.658
Just look at the size of it.

00:09:13.741 --> 00:09:15.200
The one you're holding.

00:09:15.283 --> 00:09:17.616
It would be preposterous for
that to be attached to a hood.

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:20.908
[JUDGE 204A]
Oh. Yes. Excellent point.

00:09:20.991 --> 00:09:23.325
That night, there was
one person at the temple

00:09:23.408 --> 00:09:26.658
who lost a crystal sphere
and left bloodstains. Correct?

00:09:26.741 --> 00:09:30.033
[BUTZ] Oh, is that so?
And who would that moron be?

00:09:30.116 --> 00:09:31.533
I'm surprised you asked that.

00:09:31.616 --> 00:09:34.075
I'm talking about the woman
who mentored you, moron.

00:09:34.158 --> 00:09:36.783
Ah! What? You mean Elise?

00:09:36.866 --> 00:09:39.116
[FRANZISKA]
Wait. So the victim dropped it?

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:40.575
As shown here,

00:09:40.658 --> 00:09:43.825
there's a similar crystal
sphere affixed to her cane.

00:09:43.908 --> 00:09:45.408
That may be,

00:09:45.491 --> 00:09:47.950
but do you have any actual proof
that this one belonged to her?

00:09:48.033 --> 00:09:52.033
Just look. The evidence
tells the whole story.

00:09:52.116 --> 00:09:53.033
[FRANZISKA gasps]

00:09:53.116 --> 00:09:55.241
[BUTZ]
Whoa! Her orb is gone!

00:09:55.325 --> 00:09:57.408
To make sure
I understand, Defense,

00:09:57.491 --> 00:09:59.658
are you implying it was
the victim who flew across

00:09:59.741 --> 00:10:01.075
the bridge that night?

00:10:01.158 --> 00:10:03.158
That would be
the logical conclusion.

00:10:03.241 --> 00:10:06.366
Even though, the fact remains
that humans cannot fly.

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:07.658
[CROWD gasping murmuring]

00:10:07.741 --> 00:10:09.366
[FRANZISKA]
Objection!

00:10:10.408 --> 00:10:12.950
A fool, working with
another fool on a fool's errand

00:10:13.033 --> 00:10:16.033
to foolishly reach a foolish
conclusion together.

00:10:16.116 --> 00:10:17.283
What do you mean by that?

00:10:17.366 --> 00:10:18.450
The night of the murder,

00:10:18.533 --> 00:10:20.033
Elise Deauxnim was in her room.

00:10:20.116 --> 00:10:22.116
Which is located
at Hazakura temple.

00:10:23.491 --> 00:10:26.241
She had no reason to
go to Dusky Bridge at that hour.

00:10:26.325 --> 00:10:27.325
[MILES growls]

00:10:27.408 --> 00:10:29.200
[MILES]
Unfortunately, she's correct.

00:10:29.283 --> 00:10:31.700
There's no proof that the
victim left her room that night.

00:10:31.783 --> 00:10:35.575
But, there's also
no proof she didn't.

00:10:35.658 --> 00:10:37.700
It seems that
you have nothing to say.

00:10:37.783 --> 00:10:39.616
Rare that you're speechless.

00:10:41.616 --> 00:10:44.283
[MILES] I have a hunch,
but can I prove it?

00:10:44.366 --> 00:10:48.075
No, it doesn't matter if I can.
Because I must!

00:10:49.325 --> 00:10:50.616
[MILES] After all,
that's the way Wright

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:53.908
would approach the situation.
I'm sure of it.

00:11:00.408 --> 00:11:02.700
This new evidence
points us in the direction

00:11:02.783 --> 00:11:04.241
of a new possibility.

00:11:04.325 --> 00:11:06.283
[FRANZISKA]
A new possibility?

00:11:06.366 --> 00:11:08.075
And what's that?

00:11:08.158 --> 00:11:10.491
[MILES]
Of an entirely new crime scene.

00:11:10.575 --> 00:11:12.450
She wasn't killed at the temple.

00:11:12.533 --> 00:11:15.408
Maybe... the murder was
committed next to Dusky Bridge!

00:11:15.491 --> 00:11:17.658
What? So the
scene's wrong, but ho--

00:11:17.741 --> 00:11:18.783
[yelps]

00:11:18.866 --> 00:11:20.658
How foolish! There's no way!

00:11:20.741 --> 00:11:22.366
She must've gone
down to the bridge.

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:24.283
While she was there,
something happened.

00:11:24.366 --> 00:11:27.158
And as a result, the sphere
was knocked loose.

00:11:27.241 --> 00:11:29.450
Then it somehow came
into contact with blood.

00:11:29.533 --> 00:11:32.116
And you think that
"something" was her murder?

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:35.950
The killer took her body
back to Hazakura Temple.

00:11:36.033 --> 00:11:38.533
They wanted to make it appear as
though she was murdered there.

00:11:38.616 --> 00:11:39.616
[FRANZISKA]
Objection!

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:41.033
Have you forgotten?

00:11:41.116 --> 00:11:43.783
The head nun of Hazakura
gave us her testimony earlier.

00:11:43.866 --> 00:11:45.700
She said she saw your
client killing the victim

00:11:45.783 --> 00:11:46.866
in the courtyard!

00:11:46.950 --> 00:11:48.366
[MILES]
Objection!

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:50.658
She later clarified that what
she saw, was the defendant

00:11:50.741 --> 00:11:52.116
holding on to the
weapon sticking out

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:53.366
of the victim's back.

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:55.116
Not the moment
of the actual murder!

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:56.825
[gasps]
Maybe so.

00:11:56.908 --> 00:11:59.325
But it takes ten minutes to walk
from the bridge to the temple.

00:11:59.408 --> 00:12:00.741
It's too far.

00:12:00.825 --> 00:12:01.866
The killer wouldn't
have carried

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:03.366
the body all that way.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:05.325
There was a snowmobile,
was there not?

00:12:05.408 --> 00:12:07.075
What?

00:12:07.158 --> 00:12:10.200
[MILES] They must've used
it to transport the body.

00:12:10.283 --> 00:12:13.325
Any "fool" can see that all
the pieces are in place!

00:12:13.408 --> 00:12:14.366
[CROWD gasping, murmurin]

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:16.366
[JUDGE 204A]
Order, order! Please!

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:17.491
[yelps]

00:12:17.575 --> 00:12:18.825
The defendant was
the only one who had

00:12:18.908 --> 00:12:20.408
access to the snowmobile!

00:12:20.491 --> 00:12:21.908
What's more, the witness saw her

00:12:21.991 --> 00:12:23.575
with her hands on
the murder weapon!

00:12:23.658 --> 00:12:25.783
Which leads us
to the same conclusion.

00:12:25.866 --> 00:12:28.033
That Sister Iris
is the murderer!

00:12:31.075 --> 00:12:33.408
Miss von Karma,
despite your assertions,

00:12:33.491 --> 00:12:35.491
the defense has
completed our objective.

00:12:35.575 --> 00:12:36.950
At least for the time being.

00:12:37.033 --> 00:12:39.241
What? What are you
trying to say?

00:12:39.325 --> 00:12:41.241
[MILES] We've proven it is
not possible to hand down

00:12:41.325 --> 00:12:43.158
a definite verdict
at the moment.

00:12:43.241 --> 00:12:45.575
The case requires
further investigation.

00:12:47.283 --> 00:12:48.741
We need to discover
where the murder

00:12:48.825 --> 00:12:50.075
really took place.

00:12:50.158 --> 00:12:52.075
And why the killer
needed to move the body.

00:12:52.158 --> 00:12:53.575
Also.

00:12:53.658 --> 00:12:55.700
What's actually being depicted
in the witness's artwork.

00:12:55.783 --> 00:12:57.325
Please. Don't be foolish.

00:12:57.408 --> 00:12:59.991
Do you seriously believe the
victim was somehow flying?

00:13:00.075 --> 00:13:01.616
[MILES] Her crystal sphere
was found at the foot

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:03.158
of Dusky Bridge.

00:13:03.241 --> 00:13:05.783
And her body was completely
covered in bruises indicating

00:13:05.866 --> 00:13:08.116
she fell from a sizeable height.

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:09.991
What stands out most to me

00:13:10.075 --> 00:13:12.741
is this man would never
hurt or lie about a girl

00:13:12.825 --> 00:13:13.783
with whom he is enamored.

00:13:13.866 --> 00:13:16.283
Oh. Edgy-boy.

00:13:16.366 --> 00:13:18.075
He drew what he saw then.

00:13:18.158 --> 00:13:20.116
So something had
to have happened.

00:13:22.158 --> 00:13:23.908
I hereby request
that both the defense

00:13:23.991 --> 00:13:26.783
and the prosecution conduct
further investigation.

00:13:26.866 --> 00:13:30.283
And so, with that,
court is now adjourned!

00:13:30.366 --> 00:13:33.450
[FRANZISKA growls]

00:13:33.533 --> 00:13:35.491
[MILES sighs]

00:13:35.575 --> 00:13:37.866
I've done all I can here.

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:40.741
Wright. The rest is up to you.

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:47.408
[PHOENIX]
Thanks, Miles.

00:13:47.491 --> 00:13:50.200
Way to stick to your guns.
I knew you could do it.

00:13:50.283 --> 00:13:51.825
All I did was buy more time,

00:13:51.908 --> 00:13:53.908
so we're not out
of the woods yet.

00:13:53.991 --> 00:13:55.241
Anyway...

00:13:55.325 --> 00:13:57.158
Are you sure you're
ready to leave the hospital?

00:13:57.241 --> 00:14:00.408
Not to be rude, but, uh...
You're rather green.

00:14:00.491 --> 00:14:02.450
The good news is
my fever has gone down a bit

00:14:02.533 --> 00:14:03.575
since yesterday.

00:14:03.658 --> 00:14:04.658
What's your temperature?

00:14:04.741 --> 00:14:06.491
Well, I'm finally under 102,

00:14:06.575 --> 00:14:07.783
so that's a major improvement--

00:14:07.866 --> 00:14:10.908
[coughs]

00:14:10.991 --> 00:14:14.200
[MILES sighs] So stubborn.
I've always admired that.

00:14:14.283 --> 00:14:16.200
[rasping] It's something the
two of us have in common.

00:14:16.283 --> 00:14:17.616
Indeed.

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:19.366
Which is why I can't stop
thinking about this case.

00:14:19.450 --> 00:14:21.783
The Shichishito
wasn't what killed her.

00:14:21.866 --> 00:14:23.533
So there's gotta be
another sword out there

00:14:23.616 --> 00:14:26.575
that was used. We just
need to find it somehow.

00:14:26.658 --> 00:14:28.200
That would be decisive.

00:14:28.283 --> 00:14:29.908
I'll be stopping
by the old precinct,

00:14:29.991 --> 00:14:31.991
to do some digging
on another factor.

00:14:32.075 --> 00:14:33.241
And what's that?

00:14:33.325 --> 00:14:35.116
I'm hoping to find some
more info on our client.

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:37.033
--What?
--Do you mean Iris?

00:14:37.116 --> 00:14:38.825
I can't shake
this nagging feeling

00:14:38.908 --> 00:14:42.241
that we've met before.
All I want is confirmation.

00:14:42.325 --> 00:14:44.533
[gasps]

00:14:44.616 --> 00:14:46.116
And it's perfectly
obvious that's something

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:47.616
I won't be getting from you.

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:48.991
[PHOENIX]
Hm. Yeah, sorry.

00:14:49.075 --> 00:14:51.200
Well, the rest is in your hands.

00:14:58.283 --> 00:15:00.783
So, are you about
ready to hit the road, pal?

00:15:00.866 --> 00:15:02.366
We can take my patrol car.

00:15:02.450 --> 00:15:03.866
Thanks, I appreciate it.

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:05.658
Well, it's a
necessary precaution.

00:15:05.741 --> 00:15:07.533
Gotta keep you safe
so Edgeworth's defense

00:15:07.616 --> 00:15:08.866
won't be in vain.

00:15:10.658 --> 00:15:13.575
[MILES (recording)]
Objection! Objection! Objection!

00:15:13.658 --> 00:15:17.033
Objection! Objection! Objection!

00:15:18.116 --> 00:15:21.033
Ah! Just got the news that
Dusky Bridge got patched up,

00:15:21.116 --> 00:15:23.200
so we'll finally be
able to cross over.

00:15:23.283 --> 00:15:24.325
[gasps]

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:39.075
Whoa! What the hell is that?

00:15:39.158 --> 00:15:41.950
Not quite sure,
but it wasn't here two days ago.

00:15:42.033 --> 00:15:44.658
Has anyone seen or heard
from Maya and Pearl?

00:15:44.741 --> 00:15:47.950
We haven't been able
to locate those two just yet.

00:15:48.033 --> 00:15:50.200
So they're still inside.

00:15:51.116 --> 00:15:53.741
Can you hear me?
We'll save you!

00:15:53.825 --> 00:15:55.075
[PEARL]
Mister Nick!

00:15:57.783 --> 00:15:59.325
[PHOENIX]
Oh, Pearl!

00:15:59.408 --> 00:16:01.741
I'm so glad to see you!

00:16:01.825 --> 00:16:04.408
[PEARL sobs]

00:16:08.325 --> 00:16:09.991
So you've been
over here the whole time?

00:16:10.075 --> 00:16:12.075
I was so lonely,
and so scared that I was gonna

00:16:12.158 --> 00:16:13.741
be stuck here forever.

00:16:13.825 --> 00:16:16.241
'Cause when I woke up,
the bridge wasn't there anymore,

00:16:16.325 --> 00:16:17.658
and I was by myself.

00:16:17.741 --> 00:16:19.200
That sounds scary.

00:16:19.283 --> 00:16:21.908
Hey, wait. You were alone?
Where's Maya?

00:16:21.991 --> 00:16:23.283
[PEARL whimpers]

00:16:23.366 --> 00:16:26.825
If you know where to find Maya,
you need to tell me.

00:16:26.908 --> 00:16:29.741
I... I'm sorry, Mister Nick.

00:16:29.825 --> 00:16:31.783
Uh, not your fault.

00:16:31.866 --> 00:16:33.241
[GUMSHOE]
Something smells good.

00:16:33.325 --> 00:16:34.491
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:16:34.575 --> 00:16:36.991
Like a hot, spicy,
tickle in the ol' honker.

00:16:37.075 --> 00:16:38.741
[sniffs]

00:16:38.825 --> 00:16:40.866
Wait, that's weird. Curry?

00:16:40.950 --> 00:16:42.783
[GUMSHOE]
Yeah, that's exactly what it is!

00:16:42.866 --> 00:16:44.658
Looks yummy-- I mean, yucky.

00:16:44.741 --> 00:16:47.741
My mouth's watering.
I mean, my skin's crawlin'!

00:16:47.825 --> 00:16:51.033
[PHOENIX] We all ate curry
for dinner that night.

00:16:51.116 --> 00:16:53.325
Is this the same
curry from then?

00:16:53.408 --> 00:16:54.575
Why the heck is it here?

00:16:54.658 --> 00:16:57.741
[PEARL]
Mister Nick. It is all my fault.

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:01.325
What? What is, Pearl?

00:17:01.408 --> 00:17:04.700
[sobs]
Poor Mystic Maya!

00:17:04.783 --> 00:17:06.908
Hey! Hang on! Pearl!

00:17:06.991 --> 00:17:08.408
I'll handle it, okay?

00:17:08.491 --> 00:17:10.075
You don't need
to be running around.

00:17:13.408 --> 00:17:14.783
Come on, Phoenix.

00:17:14.866 --> 00:17:17.491
This useless
schtick isn't cutting it.

00:17:17.575 --> 00:17:20.616
[sighs]
Maya needs me.

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:23.616
[GODOT] I gotta say you're
looking pathetic, Trite.

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:25.033
[PHOENIX]
Huh...?

00:17:26.533 --> 00:17:28.575
We're kinda lucky
to be here, ya know?

00:17:28.658 --> 00:17:30.491
This place has been hit
by so many earthquakes

00:17:30.575 --> 00:17:32.075
over the years that...

00:17:32.158 --> 00:17:33.825
...I wouldn't be surprised
to see it turned into a pile

00:17:33.908 --> 00:17:35.783
of rocks any day now.

00:17:35.866 --> 00:17:37.950
Didn't expect to see you.

00:17:38.033 --> 00:17:40.450
Looks like we've got
a trick lock on our hands.

00:17:40.533 --> 00:17:43.408
Only one who can open that
is the one who set it.

00:17:43.491 --> 00:17:45.366
Who could that have been?

00:17:45.450 --> 00:17:46.408
Do you know?

00:17:46.491 --> 00:17:47.658
Think about it.

00:17:47.741 --> 00:17:50.116
Who came and took over
watch for the head nun?

00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:52.283
It was Sister Iris, am I right?

00:17:52.366 --> 00:17:53.533
She locked it?

00:17:53.616 --> 00:17:55.533
I've made arrangements
for her to come here.

00:17:55.616 --> 00:17:58.450
Hopefully she'll be
showing up before much longer.

00:17:58.533 --> 00:17:59.575
[PHOENIX groans]

00:17:59.658 --> 00:18:01.866
Heh. Feeling a little woozy, eh?

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:04.033
Maybe you should go
on back to your cradle.

00:18:04.116 --> 00:18:06.408
I'll be fine. But tell me...

00:18:06.491 --> 00:18:10.241
How come you decided to
not show up to the trial today?

00:18:10.325 --> 00:18:12.825
Do you remember what
I told you in that first trial?

00:18:12.908 --> 00:18:14.283
Right at the beginning.

00:18:14.366 --> 00:18:17.033
That I would battle you
in the gladiator's arena.

00:18:17.116 --> 00:18:18.408
"The sole reason I returned from

00:18:18.491 --> 00:18:21.116
the ghastly depths of Hell."

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:24.116
Death is something
I've experienced firsthand.

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:26.241
Really? You died?

00:18:26.325 --> 00:18:29.033
In order to maintain
my new lease on life,

00:18:29.116 --> 00:18:32.283
I've gotta go through
a lot of annoying procedures.

00:18:32.366 --> 00:18:35.575
Checkups, transfusions,
more of this fluid,

00:18:35.658 --> 00:18:37.200
less of another one.

00:18:37.283 --> 00:18:39.158
Modern medicine
is a pain in the ass,

00:18:39.241 --> 00:18:41.408
but it's the only way
I can stay alive.

00:18:41.491 --> 00:18:43.075
It's just who I am now.

00:18:43.158 --> 00:18:45.866
Oh, I see.
You were in the hospital.

00:18:45.950 --> 00:18:48.200
[GODOT] Hmph. I don't wear
this mask just 'cause

00:18:48.283 --> 00:18:49.991
it looks cool, ya know?

00:18:50.075 --> 00:18:51.366
Without this thing on,

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:54.700
I can't see all those puzzled
looks on your face.

00:18:54.783 --> 00:18:57.450
But why?
What the hell happened to you?

00:18:57.533 --> 00:18:59.783
[GODOT] Tch.
You should know all this, boy.

00:18:59.866 --> 00:19:02.366
How I died.
And who it was that killed me!

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:03.741
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:19:03.825 --> 00:19:05.450
[PHOENIX] I kinda feel like
I have answers somewhere

00:19:05.533 --> 00:19:07.075
in the back of my mind.

00:19:07.158 --> 00:19:11.033
Like maybe I've heard a story
about a prosecutor dying.

00:19:15.241 --> 00:19:17.533
Wait. Hang on.

00:19:17.616 --> 00:19:20.241
Look at the base
of that lantern.

00:19:20.325 --> 00:19:22.450
There's no snow underneath it.

00:19:22.533 --> 00:19:24.325
Did somebody clear it away?

00:19:24.408 --> 00:19:25.991
That's what
was said in the trial.

00:19:26.075 --> 00:19:28.116
The defense questioned
the crime scene.

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:30.658
He said that it was
somewhere else entirely.

00:19:30.741 --> 00:19:32.616
Apparently, this is it.

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:35.908
Oh, really?
She was killed here instead.

00:19:35.991 --> 00:19:37.241
I'm worried about Maya.

00:19:37.325 --> 00:19:39.075
Stuck in there.

00:19:39.158 --> 00:19:41.991
After that rickety old
bridge finally got patched up,

00:19:42.075 --> 00:19:44.991
the cops looked all over
the Inner Temple.

00:19:45.075 --> 00:19:46.908
But there was neither
hide nor hair of her.

00:19:48.241 --> 00:19:49.741
Only place left.

00:19:49.825 --> 00:19:52.616
Would be somewhere behind that
door with the crazy lock on it.

00:19:52.700 --> 00:19:54.908
Gets really cold
inside the sacred cavern.

00:19:54.991 --> 00:19:57.908
Below freezing.
I hope she can survive.

00:19:57.991 --> 00:19:58.991
No way...

00:19:59.075 --> 00:20:01.200
And if we can't
bust her out in time,

00:20:01.283 --> 00:20:03.658
it means you sent a
woman off to die.

00:20:03.741 --> 00:20:05.533
Won't be your first one.

00:20:05.616 --> 00:20:08.866
The hell d'ya mean by that?

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:10.783
Your memory can't be so bad.

00:20:10.866 --> 00:20:12.366
Just three years ago,

00:20:12.450 --> 00:20:15.116
an innocent woman died
because of you, didn't she?

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:16.241
[gasps]

00:20:18.741 --> 00:20:20.450
Do you mean... Mia?

00:20:20.533 --> 00:20:21.700
Yeah.

00:20:21.783 --> 00:20:26.366
Maya Fey's older sister.
And your mentor, right?

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:29.366
She'd still be alive now
if it weren't for you.

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:30.658
No.

00:20:30.741 --> 00:20:32.075
[GODOT]
Three years ago,

00:20:32.158 --> 00:20:34.575
Mia made a very dangerous
person her enemy,

00:20:34.658 --> 00:20:36.783
and it cost her her life!

00:20:36.866 --> 00:20:38.366
I know.

00:20:38.450 --> 00:20:40.200
And I didn't rest until I made
sure he paid for what he did!

00:20:40.283 --> 00:20:42.283
Yeah, he may have
been caught, but so what?

00:20:42.366 --> 00:20:45.450
The truth is...
That's not gonna bring her back.

00:20:45.533 --> 00:20:47.033
[PHOENIX growls]

00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:53.033
And you...

00:20:53.116 --> 00:20:55.700
You were with her right
until that psycho killed her.

00:20:55.783 --> 00:20:57.700
It was your job to
make sure that she was safe,

00:20:57.783 --> 00:20:58.825
and you failed!

00:20:58.908 --> 00:21:00.866
[PHOENIX growls]

00:21:02.450 --> 00:21:04.908
She should've never
taken you under her wing.

00:21:04.991 --> 00:21:06.408
You're a coward!

00:21:06.491 --> 00:21:09.075
If you had any guts,
she'd be with us right now.

00:21:09.158 --> 00:21:10.616
And it's not just her!

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:13.866
You're gonna let the same thing
happen to her little sister!

00:21:13.950 --> 00:21:15.658
No... I'm not...

00:21:15.741 --> 00:21:17.658
You're just a weakling.

00:21:17.741 --> 00:21:20.950
And that's why I will never
accept you as a peer.

00:21:21.033 --> 00:21:22.325
[GODOT grunts]

00:21:27.991 --> 00:21:31.200
[PHOENIX] Maya. I can't
let her die in there.

00:21:36.200 --> 00:21:37.825
It's up to me.

00:21:42.616 --> 00:21:45.741
[PHOENIX]
What the... It can't be.

00:21:45.825 --> 00:21:47.741
I don't get it.

00:21:47.825 --> 00:21:49.616
What the hell is going on?

00:23:20.533 --> 00:23:21.991
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:23:22.075 --> 00:23:25.116
This investigation is turning up
more questions than answers.

00:23:25.200 --> 00:23:27.033
Why is Godot so against me?

00:23:27.116 --> 00:23:28.866
And what's his
connection to Mia?

00:23:28.950 --> 00:23:31.408
Meanwhile, the discovery
of new evidence puts Maya

00:23:31.491 --> 00:23:32.825
under the microscope.

00:23:32.908 --> 00:23:36.116
One after another, earth
shattering facts come to light.

00:23:36.200 --> 00:23:38.783
But what's most shocking
is who's behind it all.

00:23:38.866 --> 00:23:41.825
Profound darkness threatens
to swallow us whole.

00:23:41.908 --> 00:23:44.325
Find the contradictions!
Believe in the truth!

00:23:44.408 --> 00:23:47.575
Next episode: "Bridge to
the Turnabout - 4th Trial"!

00:23:47.658 --> 00:23:48.825
Take that!
